  triage:title "Four sqlite boundary TOMLs omit an edge that runtime-composition.toml claims they all carry" ;
  triage:description "boundary-guard BG-001 phase-ending critical review @ 9f5aef2fe. Finding: four sqlite boundary TOMLs (pending-nudge-store-sqlite, nudge-template-override-store-sqlite, graft-receiver-endpoint-store-sqlite, template-catalog-sqlite line 25) omit the forbidden atm-daemon -> atm-storage-rusqlite edge that runtime-composition.toml line 55 claims they all carry. VERIFIED: all four untouched across the full phase diff (5ad925cd7..9f5aef2fe) and no real edge exists in code. fenix's ruling: important, not blocking (no real edge exists, so this is a manifest-accuracy issue not a boundary violation); the TOML edit itself is Rand's -- agents never edit boundary TOML. Parked for Rand alongside TOML-001 (whose description boundary-guard independently confirmed complete and accurate)." ;
